      <title>PageKite: Making The Web 1000x Bigger</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Lightning Talks</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This talk briefly discusses the motivation behind the PageKite project, introduces the software itself and touches on some of the possible use cases for it.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;PageKite makes it very easy to run a publicly accessible Web server on any device, including mobile devices such as laptops or Android phones. Instead of relying on traditional dynamic DNS and manual port forwarding, Pagekite creates a zero configuration tunnel between your Web server and a remote front-end. Only the front-end has to have a route-able IP address; the server itself can reside on a heavily firewalled computer, a mobile device, or even an anonymous node on the Tor network.&lt;/p&gt;      </description>
